  "history": "Headline began in 1997 in Santa Barbara as Bertelsmann Ventures, an internet fund, and became BV Capital in 2000, with Mathias Schilling and Thomas Gieselmann among its founders, then e.ventures in 2012 and Headline in 2021. It became known for bets on Sonos, Farfetch, Bumble and Mistral AI. Today it runs early stage funds for the US, Europe, Asia and Brazil and a global growth fund, the largest of which closed at $865 million in 2024.",
